# 🏆 Section 6: Professional Mastery — Palindrome Logic

To check if a string is a palindrome (reads same forward and backward), the most efficient approach is the **Two-Pointer Method**.

### The Logic (Step-by-Step)

1. Start one pointer at index `0` and another at `length - 1`.
2. Compare characters. If they don't match, return `false`.
3. Move the start pointer forward and the end pointer backward.
4. Stop when pointers meet in the middle.

**Code Implementation:**

```java
static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
    if (str == null || str.length() == 0) return true;

    str = str.toLowerCase();
    for (int i = 0; i <= str.length() / 2; i++) {
        char start = str.charAt(i);
        char end = str.charAt(str.length() - 1 - i);

        if (start != end) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}

```

* **Time Complexity:** O(N) — We visit each character once.
* **Space Complexity:** O(1) — We don't create extra copies of the string.

